{"type":"text","timestamp":1780285698389,"sessionID":"ses_17eb4bf44ffeMqI9sk5cNK6G1O","part":{"id":"prt_e814be25e001KZvinpM0wV8kXn","sessionID":"ses_17eb4bf44ffeMqI9sk5cNK6G1O","messageID":"msg_e814bc540001eoPvnB9wx7ytcp","type":"text","text":"Done. The mechanism:\n\n- `app/actions.ts:6` — `revalidatePath('/')` is Next.js's recommended API to refresh the current page from within a Server Action. It purges the route cache so the next render (which happens automatically after the action completes) reflects the new state.\n- `app/page.tsx:11` — `<form action={toggleNotificationPreference}>` is the Server Actions pattern. Because no `redirect()` is returned, the user stays on the same page; Next.js re-renders it with the updated `enabled` value.\n- `app/store.ts` — module-level in-memory stand-in for a database call. Replace `getNotificationPreference` / `setNotificationPreference` with your real data layer.","time":{"start":1780285698386,"end":1780285698386}}}
